ALL = ' And all that is required to complete the work fully ready for operation in accordance with the drawings and specifications, even if not expressly stated.'
SIG = ' The Contractor shall comply with the Al Ahsa Health Cluster digital signage standard AAHC-FM-STD-DIGITAL-SIGNAGE-001: commercial displays designed for continuous operation (Samsung QMC or approved equivalent, and QHC for high‑ambient‑light areas) with 4K UHD resolution as a minimum, consumer televisions not being accepted in public areas; displays in public areas connected to the Navori platform with a built‑in or external player; two power sockets behind each display (one on emergency power/UPS where possible) and a wired RJ45 network point; all cables concealed behind the display or in approved containment; and sizes and mounting heights per the tables of the standard.'
T = {
'LS-81': ('Earthing System', 'Supply, installation and testing of the complete earthing system (ABB or VERSE): earth pits with 3 m long, 20 mm diameter copper rods, 70 mm² bare copper conductor, clamps, test links and earth bars, and exothermic welding where required; with a resistance not exceeding 4 ohms for the power system and an independent system for low current not exceeding 2 ohms; earthing of AC compressors and roof equipment, and earthing of medical equipment per IEC 60364‑7‑710; adding pits or soil enhancer where needed to achieve the required values for the saline nature of Al Ahsa soil without additional claim; and measurement of each system separately with approved reports.' + ALL),
'LS-82': ('Uninterruptible Power Supply (UPS)', 'Supply, installation and commissioning of an industrial on‑line double‑conversion UPS of not less than 10 kVA (EATON or equivalent) feeding critical loads only (medical systems, servers, emergency lighting and dedicated outlets), with a battery bank running the full load for at least one hour per a documented calculation in an air‑conditioned location, monitoring panel and display, static bypass and maintenance bypass, input and output cables, isolators and earthing; with full‑load, battery autonomy, transfer and bypass tests, factory certificates and warranty.' + ALL),
'LS-83': ('Structured Cabling and Wireless Access Points', 'Supply, installation and testing of the centre’s structured cabling per TIA/EIA‑568: flush Cat6A data points (Legrand) with horizontal cables of the same category, and fibre optic cables for the backbone; managed PoE network switches (Huawei), Cat6A patch panels, patch cords, cable managers and fibre distribution units; network cabinets with power distribution units, fans, doors, earthing and professional cable management; wireless access points at the specified locations; containment segregated from power cables; certification testing of every point with a cable certifier and of fibres with an OTDR, labelling matching the cable schedule, and handover of certification reports, as‑built drawings and operating manuals.' + ALL),
'LS-84': ('IP‑PBX and Telephone Sets', 'Supply, installation and configuration of an AVAYA IP Office 500 PBX with an Essential Edition licence supporting 50 IP extensions and voice compression modules (VCM), standard and video telephone sets in the specified quantities with 3 m patch cables, the necessary network switches, and a floor cabinet with four fans, a 6‑way power distribution unit, two vertical cable managers and two shelves; programming of numbering plans, hunt groups, voicemail and call forwarding, connection of external lines and the structured cabling; and testing, documentation and training of users and the IT team.' + ALL),
'LS-85': ('Public Address and Display Screens', 'Supply, installation and testing of the public address and voice evacuation system (Bosch Praesideo/Plena or DSPPA): central rack and amplifiers with capacities covering all zones, the control unit and paging microphone at reception, ceiling speakers and volume controls, and division into independent paging zones, with fire‑resistant low‑smoke (LSZH) cables, interfaced with the fire alarm for evacuation messages; testing of coverage and sound level in each zone; and supply and installation of display screens in the specified sizes and locations with their brackets and connections.' + ALL + SIG),
'LS-86': ('Addressable Fire Alarm System', 'Supply, installation, commissioning and testing of an addressable fire alarm system (Gent by Honeywell) approved by Civil Defense: a main control panel with loops and standby batteries per code, smoke and heat detectors and duct smoke detectors, manual call points, audible and visual alarm devices, and monitor, control and short‑circuit isolator modules; interfaces with HVAC (unit shutdown and fire damper closure), public address (voice evacuation), the automatic door, emergency bars, the elevator, the air curtain and the clean agent suppression; with LSZH fire‑resistant cables segregated from power; and full testing in the presence of the supervision and Civil Defense and obtaining final approval.' + ALL),
'LS-87': ('CCTV System', 'Supply, installation and testing of a digital CCTV system (Hikvision Ultra Series Smart IP): 8 MP day/night cameras with infrared, internal domes and external bullet or PTZ cameras with IP66 protection, PoE powered; a network video recorder (NVR) with surveillance‑grade disks sized for the required retention period, monitors in the control room, and PoE switches (Huawei); with Belden Cat6A cables, brackets and conduits; and testing of day and night image clarity, coverage angles and actual storage duration.' + ALL),
'LS-88': ('Nurse Call System', 'Supply, installation and commissioning of a wireless nurse call system for healthcare facilities (SOLT or equivalent): a central control unit and nurse stations with displays or annunciator panels showing the call source audibly and visually, bedside call points and emergency pull cords in toilets, colour‑coded dome lights outside rooms, and transmitters, receivers and repeaters ensuring full coverage without dead spots; with testing of every point, response time and coverage, and training of nursing staff.' + ALL),
'LS-89': ('Kerbs, Pavements, Interlock and Stone', 'Supply and installation of 50×30×15 cm chamfered precast concrete kerbs on 7 cm concrete and a 20 cm base layer around roads, parking and planters (Riyadh, Tamimi or equivalent); interlock paving 8 cm thick, and 10 cm under parking, in the shapes and sizes of the approved sample on 10 cm plain concrete with expansion joints and compaction; warning and guidance tactile tiles for the visually impaired from the accessible parking bay to the entrance per the universal access guide; natural stone or premium granite for the front entrance area as per drawings; and ramps and external handrails where specified.' + ALL),
'LS-90': ('Asphalt Paving and Parking Marking', 'Supply and execution of asphalt works for the general site: a 30 cm base course compacted to not less than 95% density, MC1 prime coat, a first 7 cm asphalt layer, RC2 tack coat and a 5 cm wearing course with an asphalt grade suitable for Al Ahsa temperatures, at levels and falls (not less than 1%) achieving storm water drainage; density testing of each layer at an accredited laboratory; and marking of parking bays and accessible bays with their signs, and wheel stops per the approved sample.' + ALL),
'LS-91': ('Landscaping and Irrigation Network', 'Execution of the green‑area design approved by an office accredited by the Engineering Department; supply and installation of the irrigation network in 10‑bar HDPE or UPVC of calculated sizes at a depth of not less than 60 cm with special fittings, backfilling with fine sand and testing, solenoid valves (RainBird exclusively) with their boxes, control wiring and the central controller, sprinklers and drippers; and supply and planting of salt‑ and heat‑tolerant, water‑saving plants per an approved planting schedule, tested salt‑free agricultural soil, fertilizer and decorative stones, by a specialist company, with watering and maintenance until provisional acceptance.' + ALL),
'LS-92': ('Utility Connections and Permits', 'Application and follow‑up with the Saudi Electricity Company, the National Water Company, the municipality and competent authorities in the project’s name; payment of all connection, meter and deposit fees; preparation of the transformer room or connection point per Saudi Electricity Company requirements; and construction of service lines from the public networks to the building: power up to the connection point, water from the meter to the underground tank, sewage and storm water to the public network (or a septic tank depending on availability and municipality requirements), and telecom and fibre cable to the telecom room; including excavation, backfilling and reinstatement of streets and pavements, testing, and obtaining connection records and completion certificates from the authorities before provisional acceptance.' + ALL),
'LS-93': None,  # same as LS-34
'LS-94': ('Medical Equipment', 'Supply, installation and commissioning of medical equipment for a primary healthcare (family medicine) centre for all clinics and departments shown on the drawings; the Contractor shall determine quantities from the drawings for each space. It includes, without limitation: each clinic: an electric or hydraulic examination couch with step, a wall‑ or stand‑mounted digital blood pressure monitor, a wall diagnostic set (otoscope and ophthalmoscope with rechargeable handles), an examination lamp, a scale and height measure, a stethoscope, and the examination curtain (under the curtains item); vital signs: a vital signs monitor (BP, pulse, temperature, SpO₂), an adult digital scale with height rod, and an infant scale and length board; emergency and dressing: an equipped crash cart, an automated external defibrillator (AED) or defibrillator with display, a portable suction unit, a 12‑lead ECG, a nebulizer, a portable oxygen cylinder on a trolley with regulator, an emergency bed or stretcher with side rails, a stainless dressing trolley, an IV stand and a wheelchair; phlebotomy and vaccination: a phlebotomy chair with arm rests, a medical vaccine refrigerator with temperature logger and alarm per cold‑chain requirements, a medical drug refrigerator, and a glucometer; sterilization: a benchtop steam autoclave of suitable size, a sealer, and shelving and trolleys for clean and soiled instruments; and whatever appears on the drawings or the departmental equipment list (such as a dental clinic or laboratory, if any) with their standard equipment. All devices shall be new and registered with the Saudi FDA (MDMA) through an authorized agent in the Kingdom, with technical data and catalogues approved by the Medical Equipment and Biomedical Engineering sections before supply; including installation, commissioning, calibration and calibration certificates, electrical safety tests, training of users and biomedical technicians, operation and maintenance manuals, a warranty of not less than two years with preventive maintenance during the warranty and spare parts availability for not less than 7 years, and registration of the devices in the asset register before acceptance.' + ALL),
}
